## feat(ontology-ui): add key_column field to Dataset panel

**Context:** The Dataset section of the ontology class Actions panel needed a "Key column" input so users can specify which UC table column maps to the node ID. This is Task 1 of the MCP node-context feature (key_column flows through to Task 2's backend round-trip).

**Changes:**
1. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js` — Added `key_column: null` to `sharedPanelDataset` object in `_datasetSelectAsset` (line ~1188).
2. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js` — Replaced `renderSharedEntityDataset` body to render a `<input id="datasetKeyColumnInput">` below the asset display when not in view-only mode; shows read-only `<code>` snippet in view-only mode.
3. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js` — Added `onDatasetKeyColumnChange(value)` handler immediately after `renderSharedEntityDataset`.

**Modified files:**
- `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js`

**Test result:** No automated tests cover JS UI in this repo. Manual inspection confirms balanced braces, correct template literals, and that `key_column` flows through the existing save payload (`dataset: sharedPanelDataset || undefined`) without additional changes.
